## 3. Hardware Component Calculations

### Scenario A: High-Impedance Load (Oscilloscope / >10 MΩ)

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| PSU | +8 V DC |
| R_pull | 220 Ω (0.25 W) |
| Output | ±4 V AC via C1 |

### Scenario B: Low-Impedance Load (45 Ω Handset Speaker)

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| PSU | +16 V DC |
| R_pull | 47 Ω (≥2 W) |
| Output | ≈ ±3.9 V AC |

$$U_{\text{max}} = 16\text{V} \times \frac{45\,\Omega}{47\,\Omega + 45\,\Omega} \approx 7.8\text{V}$$

**C1:** 10 – 47 µF electrolytic, ≥25 V (50 V recommended). Positive pin to MOSFET Drain, negative to output.

